IMPORT prelude

-- Legal Aid and Advice Act 1995 (Singapore) -- who may get civil legal aid and for what (s 5 and the Schedule), how a Grant of Aid
-- is decided (s 8), whose means are looked at when the applicant is a minor (s 6(4), (5)), the 14-day stay of the other side's case
-- (ss 10(3), 17), what a filed Grant of Aid spares the aided person (s 12(4), (5)), the deposit for out-of-pocket expenses (s 13),
-- costs and contributions taken out of what is recovered (ss 16(3), (4), 22A(3), (4)), appeals (s 18), legal advice (s 20), the
-- offence of misstating means (s 21), and the limit of privilege (s 22(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/12/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/LAAA1995.txt. The revised edition incorporates amendments to 1 December 2021; later amendments are
-- annotated in the text, the latest being Act 32 of 2024 (in force 1 April 2025) and Act 31 of 2023 (s 5(6), in force
-- 1 December 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: it decides who can get a state-funded lawyer
-- for a divorce, a maintenance claim, a work injury claim or a civil suit, and who can get free legal advice. SCOPED to the
-- provisions an applicant or aided person meets. Not encoded: the appointment of the Director and the solicitor panels (ss 3, 4,
-- 4A), professional deputies (s 6A), the Director's inquiry powers (s 7), the Minister's authorised persons (s 8(5)-(7)),
-- applications by both sides (s 11), assignment and filing mechanics (s 12(1)-(3), (6)), court-ordered costs against an aided person
-- (s 14), discharge of the solicitor (s 15), the costs rules of s 16(1), (2), (5)-(7), rules of court (s 19), recovery as a debt
-- (s 22B), and the regulations (s 23). THE MEANS TEST ITSELF IS PRESCRIBED BY REGULATIONS, WHICH WERE NOT RETRIEVED: here it is a
-- bare yes/no.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Aid and Advice Act 1995 -- legal aid`

DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `a citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a foreigner resident in Singapore`
    `a foreigner not resident in Singapore`

DECLARE Proceeding IS ONE OF
    `a divorce under the Women's Charter`
    `a High Court civil claim`
    `a District Court civil claim`
    `a Syariah Court case`
    `a work injury claim before the Commissioner for Labour`
    `a High Court defamation claim`
    `a breach of promise of marriage claim in a District Court`
    `a relator action`
    `an election petition`
    `a District Court defence about only the time or mode of paying a debt`
    `a criminal charge in a District Court`

§§ `5 and the Schedule -- who, and for what`

-- s 5(1): "legal aid may be given to a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore in relation to any civil proceedings mentioned in
-- Part 1 of the Schedule (not being any proceedings mentioned in Part 2 of the Schedule)." (2): the Director may authorise legal aid
-- for Part 2 proceedings "if the Director is satisfied that those proceedings are, or are likely to be, related to" Part 1
-- proceedings. (4): the list may be varied by regulations (none retrieved).
-- Schedule Part 1: proceedings in the High Court divisions and Court of Appeal (1); Family Courts, District Courts, Magistrates'
-- Courts (2); references (3, 4); "Proceedings under the Women's Charter 1961" (5); the Syariah Court (6); the Commissioner for Labour
-- under the Work Injury Compensation Act (7).
-- Schedule Part 2, "PROCEEDINGS FOR WHICH LEGAL AID IS GENERALLY NOT GIVEN": proceedings wholly or partly in respect of defamation,
-- breach of promise of marriage, or inducing a spouse to leave (1); relator actions (2); applications under the Parliamentary or
-- Presidential Elections Acts (3); in a Family or District Court, judgment summons proceedings and a defendant's proceedings "where the
-- only question ... is as to the time or mode of payment by him or her of a debt" (4); incidental proceedings (5).
-- A criminal charge is heard in a District Court (Part 1 item 2) but s 5(1) is confined to CIVIL proceedings; Part 2 of the Act is
-- headed "LEGAL AID IN CIVIL ACTIONS".
GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeding is in Part 1 of the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the proceeding`
    WHEN `a criminal charge in a District Court` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a relator action` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an election petition` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeding is in Part 2 of the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the proceeding`
    WHEN `a High Court defamation claim` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a breach of promise of marriage claim in a District Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a relator action` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an election petition` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a District Court defence about only the time or mode of paying a debt` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the applicant's status` IS A Status, `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding, `the Director is satisfied it relates to a Part 1 proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `legal aid may be given for the proceeding` IF
        (`the applicant's status` EQUALS `a citizen` OR `the applicant's status` EQUALS `a permanent resident`)
    AND (    (`the proceeding is in Part 1 of the Schedule` `the proceeding` AND (NOT `the proceeding is in Part 2 of the Schedule` `the proceeding`))
         OR  (`the proceeding is in Part 2 of the Schedule` `the proceeding` AND `the Director is satisfied it relates to a Part 1 proceeding`))

§§ `8 -- the Grant of Aid`

-- s 8(1): the Director may issue a Grant of Aid if "(a) the Director is of the opinion that the applicant satisfies the prescribed
-- means criteria; and (b)" reasonable grounds for "taking, defending, continuing or being a party to those proceedings" -- judged by
-- the Director for prescribed proceedings (i), and otherwise by "a board (consisting of the Director and at least 2 solicitors on an
-- appropriate panel ...)" (ii).
-- (3): the Director "may refuse legal aid if it appears to the Director unreasonable" (a discretion; not modelled -- "may" is read
-- as permission, not entitlement).
-- (4) "Despite any provision of this Act": the Minister may (a) authorise a Grant of Aid to any person "in the public interest"; (b)
-- direct a grant "even though the Director is of the opinion that the applicant does not satisfy ... the prescribed means criteria,
-- if the Minister is of the opinion that it is just and proper". (4)(b) directs a grant "under subsection (1) or (2)", so the merits
-- limb still applies to it (an inference from that cross-reference).
GIVEN `meets the means criteria` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the proceedings are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director finds reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the board finds reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister directs despite means` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister authorises in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Grant of Aid may be issued` IF
        `the Minister authorises in the public interest`
    OR  (    (`meets the means criteria` OR `the Minister directs despite means`)
         AND (    (`the proceedings are prescribed` AND `the Director finds reasonable grounds`)
              OR  ((NOT `the proceedings are prescribed`) AND `the board finds reasonable grounds`)))

-- s 8(2): pending determination, a provisional Grant of Aid if the applicant "(a) requires legal aid as a matter of urgency; (b) is
-- likely to satisfy the prescribed means criteria; and (c) is likely to have reasonable grounds".
GIVEN `urgent` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to meet the means criteria` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to have reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provisional Grant of Aid may be issued` IF
    `urgent` AND `likely to meet the means criteria` AND `likely to have reasonable grounds`

§§ `6(3)-(5) and 22A(2) -- a minor's application`

-- s 6(3): a minor's application "must be made on behalf of the minor by the minor's guardian". (4)(b): for the means test in
-- s 8(1)(a), (2)(b), the applicant means, "in any case where the minor is unmarried and the guardian is a relative of the minor ...
-- both the guardian and the minor and in every other case ... the minor only". (5): "relative" means "(a) in the case of a legitimate
-- child, any one of his or her parents; (b) in the case of an adopted child, an adopting parent; and (c) in the case of an
-- illegitimate child, the mother." s 22A(2) uses the same test for who pays a contribution.
DECLARE Guardian IS ONE OF
    `a parent of a legitimate child`
    `an adopting parent of an adopted child`
    `the mother of an illegitimate child`
    `the father of an illegitimate child`
    `a grandparent`

DECLARE MeansBasis IS ONE OF
    `the guardian and the minor`
    `the minor only`

GIVEN `the guardian` IS A Guardian
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the guardian is a relative` IF
    CONSIDER `the guardian`
    WHEN `the father of an illegitimate child` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a grandparent` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the guardian` IS A Guardian, `the minor is married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MeansBasis
`whose means are tested` MEANS
    IF `the guardian is a relative` `the guardian` AND (NOT `the minor is married`)
    THEN `the guardian and the minor`
    ELSE `the minor only`

§§ `10(3) and 17 -- the 14-day stay`

-- s 17(1): where proceedings have begun and a party applies for legal aid, the Director must notify the other parties and file a
-- notification with the court. (2): "unless the court ... orders otherwise", "all steps in those proceedings are stayed for a period of
-- 14 days after the date on which the notification is filed" and time does not run. (3): the filing "does not prevent" (a) an
-- interlocutory injunction or the appointment of a receiver or manager; (b) an order preventing the lapse of a caveat against dealings
-- with land; (c) any other order "necessary to prevent an irremediable injustice"; (d) proceedings to enforce those orders. (4): the
-- 14 days may be reduced or extended by the court.
-- s 10(3): the same 14-day stay follows a notification that a Grant of Aid has been CANCELLED. Section 10 has no counterpart to
-- s 17(3). Days are counted here as whole days after the filing date (a reading; the text does not say how to count).
DECLARE Trigger IS ONE OF
    `a notification of an application for legal aid`
    `a notification of cancellation of a Grant of Aid`

DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary step in the action`
    `an interlocutory injunction`
    `an order preventing a caveat from lapsing`
    `an order to prevent an irremediable injustice`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step is protected by section 17(3)` IF
    NOT (`the step` EQUALS `an ordinary step in the action`)

GIVEN `the trigger` IS A Trigger, `the step` IS A Step, `days after filing` IS A NUMBER, `the stay period in days` IS A NUMBER, `the court ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step is stayed` IF
        (NOT `the court ordered otherwise`)
    AND `days after filing` AT MOST `the stay period in days`
    AND (    `the trigger` EQUALS `a notification of cancellation of a Grant of Aid`
         OR  (NOT `the step is protected by section 17(3)` `the step`))

§§ `12(4), (5) -- what a filed Grant of Aid spares the aided person`

-- s 12(4): once the Grant of Aid is filed, the aided person "(a) is not liable ... for court fees or for such fees payable for the
-- service of process or for any fees due to the Sheriff or bailiff"; "(b) is entitled to be supplied free of charge with a copy of the
-- judge's notes of evidence"; "(c) is not, except where express provision is made in this Act, liable for costs to any other party";
-- "(d) is not liable to pay any deposit which would have been payable to the Official Assignee" where aid was granted to commence
-- bankruptcy proceedings against a debtor.
-- (5): "Subject to sections 13 and 22A", no investigating or assigned solicitor may "take or agree to take or seek from an aided person
-- any fee, profit or reward". Section 13 (a deposit for out-of-pocket expenses) and s 22A (contributions) are what the aided person
-- may still be asked to pay.
DECLARE Payment IS ONE OF
    `court fees`
    `fees for service of process`
    `Sheriff or bailiff fees`
    `a copy of the judge's notes of evidence`
    `the other party's costs`
    `the Official Assignee's deposit on a bankruptcy application`
    `a fee to the assigned solicitor`
    `a deposit for out-of-pocket expenses`
    `a contribution required by the Director`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the filed Grant of Aid spares the aided person` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a deposit for out-of-pocket expenses` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contribution required by the Director` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `13(2), (3) -- the deposit for out-of-pocket expenses`

-- s 13(1): the Director may require a deposit towards "out-of-pocket expenses (not including office expenses)". (2): it "must be used
-- only to pay -- (a) firstly, the out-of-pocket expenses ...; and (b) after the payment of such out-of-pocket expenses, any outstanding
-- contribution". (3): "the balance ... (if any) must be refunded". (4): where a deposit "would occasion hardship" the Director may meet
-- the expenses instead (not modelled).
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`at least nil` MEANS IF `x` AT LEAST 0 THEN `x` ELSE 0

GIVEN `the deposit` IS A NUMBER, `the out-of-pocket expenses` IS A NUMBER, `the outstanding contribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund of the deposit` MEANS
    `at least nil` (`at least nil` (`the deposit` MINUS `the out-of-pocket expenses`) MINUS `the outstanding contribution`)

§§ `16(3), (4) and 22A(3), (4) -- what comes out of a recovery`

-- s 16(3): where an aided person recovers money "(whether in proceedings or by virtue of a settlement or compromise)", the aided
-- person "is liable to pay to the Director so much of the moneys so recovered as is recovered in respect of costs". (4): the costs part
-- is "deemed to be so much of the total amount so recovered as exceeds the amount (if any) recoverable by the aided person otherwise
-- than as costs". (7): the Director may reduce, waive or refund (not modelled).
GIVEN `the total recovered` IS A NUMBER, `the amount recoverable otherwise than as costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the costs payable to the Director` MEANS
    `at least nil` (`the total recovered` MINUS `the amount recoverable otherwise than as costs`)

-- s 22A(3): "Unless the regulations ... provide otherwise, any sum remaining unpaid on account of a person's contribution ... may be
-- deducted from any property that is recovered or preserved for that person". (4): that property includes settlement rights and
-- damages or costs recovered "(other than any sums payable to the Director under section 14 or 16)", "but excludes ... any compensation
-- paid or payable to the person under the Work Injury Compensation Act 2019". (5): set-off by the court is preserved (not modelled).
-- Encoded as the most that MAY be deducted; whether to deduct is the Director's call (s 22A(6) also allows reduction or waiver).
GIVEN `the property recovered net of sums payable under section 16` IS A NUMBER, `the unpaid contribution` IS A NUMBER, `it is work injury compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be deducted for the contribution` MEANS
    IF `it is work injury compensation`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the smaller of` (`at least nil` `the property recovered net of sums payable under section 16`) (`at least nil` `the unpaid contribution`)

§§ `18 -- appeals`

-- s 18(1): an aided person who wishes to appeal after the proceedings were heard "must make a fresh application for legal aid ...
-- within the prescribed time", and the s 8 conditions apply afresh. (2): the Director may consider a late application if "(a) the aided
-- person filed a notice of appeal ... before making that application; or (b) ... there are extenuating circumstances". (3): (1) "does
-- not apply to an appeal in respect of any interlocutory matter". The prescribed time is in regulations (not retrieved).
GIVEN `the appeal is interlocutory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fresh application is needed for the appeal` IF
    NOT `the appeal is interlocutory`

GIVEN `made within the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN, `a notice of appeal was filed first` IS A BOOLEAN, `extenuating circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may consider the appeal application` IF
    `made within the prescribed time` OR `a notice of appeal was filed first` OR `extenuating circumstances`

§§ `20 -- legal advice`

-- s 20(1): "legal advice is available to persons resident and present in Singapore" -- no citizenship or permanent residence
-- requirement, unlike legal aid under s 5. (2): oral advice on matters that may lead to legal-aid proceedings, help preparing documents,
-- or prescribed matters, "but does not include any advice ... in respect of any law that is not the law of Singapore". (4): the person
-- "must satisfy the Director that the person cannot afford to obtain the legal advice in the ordinary way".
GIVEN `resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `present in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `cannot afford advice in the ordinary way` IS A BOOLEAN, `the question is about foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `legal advice may be given` IF
    `resident in Singapore` AND `present in Singapore` AND `cannot afford advice in the ordinary way` AND (NOT `the question is about foreign law`)

§§ `21 -- false statements and undisclosed means`

-- s 21: a person seeking or receiving legal aid or legal advice who "(a) knowingly makes any false or misleading statement or
-- representation in the person's application ...; (b) fails to make full and frank disclosure of the person's means; or (c) fails to
-- inform the Director of any changes to the person's means or circumstances which may render the person ineligible for legal aid" is
-- guilty of an offence: "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both".
-- Only (a) says "knowingly"; (b) and (c) carry no mental element on their face.
GIVEN `made a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to disclose means fully and frankly` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to report a change that may make them ineligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 21 is committed` IF
        (`made a false or misleading statement` AND `knew it was false or misleading`)
    OR  `failed to disclose means fully and frankly`
    OR  `failed to report a change that may make them ineligible`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 21 in dollars` MEANS 5000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment under section 21 in months` MEANS 6

§§ `22 -- privilege`

-- s 22(1): the privileges of client and solicitor arise between an applicant, aided person or advice-seeker and the Director and the
-- solicitor. (2): "Despite anything in subsection (1), the privileges ... are not to arise in relation to any information tendered to
-- the Director concerning the property or income of the applicant for a Grant of Aid."
DECLARE Information IS ONE OF
    `the applicant's account of the dispute`
    `the applicant's statement of property and income`
    `advice given by the assigned solicitor`

GIVEN `the information` IS A Information
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `privilege attaches to the information` IF
    NOT (`the information` EQUALS `the applicant's statement of property and income`)
